--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description:
libnvv4l2.so is the DeepStream build of libv4l2 (from v4l-utils). It is the
userspace V4L2 wrapper (v4l2_open / v4l2_ioctl and format conversion) used by
the gst-v4l2 plugin. nvv4l2decoder in libgstnvvideo4linux2.so links
-lnvv4l2 from /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/.

libnvv4l2.so links -lnvv4lconvert (-L../libv4lconvert). Build and install
../libv4lconvert before this directory. See ../README.

The library sources are LGPL-2.1-or-later. This README is Apache-2.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Platform:
x86_64 only. The Makefile stops on any other architecture, including Jetson.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- DeepStream SDK installed, so the install directory exists
- gcc
- libnvv4lconvert.so already built in ../libv4lconvert (and installed before
  this library is used at runtime)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the library (from this directory):

  $ make && sudo make install

Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).

The default install directory is /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/.
make install copies libnvv4l2.so there and adds a libv4l2.so.0 symlink to it.

To install somewhere else:

  $ make install LIB_INSTALL_DIR=<dir>/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verify:

  $ ldd /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/libnvv4l2.so

ldd should resolve libnvv4lconvert.so. After gst-v4l2 is also installed:

  $ gst-inspect-1.0 nvv4l2decoder
